    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278">

                <pb facs="0541" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p1/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.5851G/9–2451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Legation at Saigon </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-24T20:00:00-04:00">September 24,
                            1951—8 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>424. During course dinner conversation with de Lattre Sep 23, Merchant asked de
                    Lattre status in intern KMT troops in Indochina and prospect their repatriation
                    Formosa. Recognizing US interest in accomplishing repatriation, Gen stated
                    emphatically that in view existing threat Chi Communist intervention he must
                    avoid any action which cld be considered by Commies or by others as provocative,
                        <pb facs="0542" n="524" xml:id="pg524"/> which he believed repatriation wld
                    be. He added he found presence KMT troops expensive and source of difficulties
                    with local population.</p>
                <p>Sent to AmLegation Saigon, for info 424, AmEmbassy Paris, for info 1780,
                    AmEmbassy Taipei, for info 265.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
